    "description": "Natural Mineral Specimen Lot of 2\nAmethyst Quartz Cluster & Cut Base Green Fluorite\n2 Pieces\nThis lot of two natural geological specimens features an amethyst quartz crystal geode cluster and a substantial rough green fluorite display piece with a sawn flat base. The amethyst specimen exhibits lavender to violet crystalline points resting atop a layered agate and basalt matrix band. The companion green fluorite specimen displays pale seafoam to emerald-green translucent crystalline mass with natural rough cleavage and mineral veining, cut flat on the bottom and back for upright shelf or tabletop display.\nIncludes two distinct natural mineral display specimens\nAmethyst cluster features defined crystalline druzy terminations and agate banding\nGreen fluorite specimen features cut flat base and back for stable freestanding display\nSuitable for mineral collectors, lapidary display, or natural interior accents\nCondition:\nVery good natural condition. Amethyst points are largely intact with minor natural edge wear and matrix inclusions. Green fluorite shows natural crystalline cleavage planes, internal fractures, and rough matrix crust consistent with natural raw stone.\nPOLICIES and Seller Info\nHow to reach us-\nPer the policies of our selling location, we do not remove unpaid items or cancel bids. Thank you for understanding!\nSending a message via shopgoodwill.com message is the only way to reach us and receive a response. Your concerns are very important to us, but we do not have a business phone on site. Calls to the home office cannot be transferred to us, so if you call and leave a message, you are guaranteed NOT to receive a response and we don't want that! Customer services messages are checked throughout the day, Monday through Friday (excluding holidays), between the hours of 9am and 4pm eastern time.\nDomestic Shipping-\nItems with a Fixed/Flat shipping fee (rather than calculated) will ship the cheapest possible way, FedEx shipping is not guaranteed on items with a fixed shipping cost. FedEx does not ship to P.O. boxes or APO/FPO addresses. Please enter an address that we can ship to at check out.\nYour package will be insured, regardless of mail class or carrier, however, insurance DOES NOT cover theft after delivery. Porch piracy is very common so we strongly suggest that you use your DAYTIME address you will be available to receive your package. If you require a specific carrier, signature confirmation, or have a special packing/handling request, please make your needs known by clicking Contact Seller prior to making payment so that we can add applicable fees for service(s) requested. We have accounts with FedEx and USPS only.\nHandling-\nItems like instruments, artwork, delicate collectibles, stereo receivers, and sewing machines require additional packing materials and labor to pack them safely. For this reason, handling fees are higher on specialty items.\nHandling fees cap at $15 on combined orders. So if you combine 10 items with a $2 each handling fee, the system will automatically discount your shipping price and your handling would be $15 rather than $20. (This applies to items combined from Chattanooga Area Goodwill only).\nGeneral Disclaimers-\nAll items are donated and in used condition unless otherwise specified. Please manage your expectations accordingly.\nColors may vary depending on the settings of your monitor. Items are measured by hand, and are may vary by 1-3cm.\nAll items have potentially been exposed to pets and/or other allergens. Returns are not authorized for odors, ever, under any circumstance. If you are sensitive to allergens and/or odors, we recommend that you not purchase pre-owned items.\nWe typically do not authorize returns, so it is VERY important that you read the full description, carefully view all photos, and ask any questions you may have PRIOR to placing bids. Pictures are considered a part of the item description. Any item returned without prior authorization from the seller will be considered a donation and re-sold.\nSpecial Disclaimers (\nwhenever applicable\n)-\nOur Presidium Gem Tester is able to identify the gemstone family or families based on the hardness of the tested gem. We are not certified gemologists, so we are not always able to determine the specific gemstone(s) present, differentiate between certain stones, or confirm the device's findings.\nMost of the world's pearls are cultured. The ability to differentiate between cultured, freshwater, and natural (ocean) pearls is beyond the scope of our equipment.\nUnless otherwise stated above, all marked metals are tested by our Thermo Scientific Niton DXL Precious Metal Analyzer. Photos will be provided in listing of results. If not, a precious metal it will be listed and Gold/Silver Tone or plated.\nSome listings may contain a mixture of fine jewelry AND costume jewelry. Please read full description to understand what you are buying. Items described as costume jewelry are presumed to not include precious metals, regardless of any markings you may see in photos.\nLocal Pick Up-\nWe do not have local pickup. All items will be shipped.  If you'd like to have it shipped to your place of business instead of a residential address. Please contact us with any shipping questions.\nInternational Shipping-\nINTERNATIONAL BUYERS' OUTSIDE OF THE USA AND CANADA are not eligible for any shipping discounts including flat rate or penny shipping. Contact us via Shopgoodwill.com message for an estimate prior to bidding on any items with discounted shipping.",
