    "description": "Brazilian Agate Geode Bookend\nPolished Natural Agate with Blue Enhancement\nMid-to-Late 20th Century Lapidary Decor\nThis natural Brazilian agate geode section has been cut and polished to highlight intricate concentric banding and a crystalline quartz core, enhanced with a vibrant blue dye treatment. Popularized during the mid-to-late 20th century as functional desk accessories and display specimens, cut geode bookends highlight organic geological formations alongside geometric lapidary craftsmanship.\nNatural agate geode featuring fine banding surrounding a crystalline quartz center\nPolished front face and upright surface with preserved natural rough rind on the exterior\nEquipped with three protective green felt pads on the base to prevent surface scratching\nMeasures approximately 5 inches tall, 3.5 inches long, and 2.5 inches wide, weighing 2.1 lbs\nCondition:\nVery good vintage condition. The polished faces display a smooth, lustrous finish with clearly defined banding. The rough exterior shows typical geological texture and variations inherent to natural stone formation. Base felt pads are intact. Free of chips, cracks, or damage beyond natural mineral characteristics.\nTHANK YOU FOR SUPPORTING OUR MISSION!\nIf there is a problem with your order, please contact us via Shop Goodwill before opening returns/claims. We strive to respond to all inquiries within 2 business days.\nOur business hours are Monday - Friday  7:00 am to 3:00 pm EST\n**If your item was damaged in transit, do not throw away anything, including the box or packing materials until we have authorized you to do so.\n**Photos will be required to file insurance claims.\nGoodwill of Western and Northern Connecticut strengthens communities by helping people with disabilities and other disadvantages maximize independence through job training and other support services.",
